{"sections":{"breadcrumbs_DgnWDV":{"type":"breadcrumbs","disabled":true,"settings":{"container":"fixed","text_alignment":"start","padding_top":20,"padding_bottom":20}},"main":{"type":"main-page","disabled":true,"settings":{"container":"fixed","text_alignment":"center","padding_top":28,"padding_bottom":28}},"spacer_EEpi9n":{"type":"spacer","name":"t:sections.spacer.name","settings":{"show_section_divider":false,"divider_width":"fixed","padding_top":50,"padding_bottom":50,"padding_top_mobile":24,"padding_bottom_mobile":24}},"rich_text_kyFd96":{"type":"rich-text","blocks":{"subheading_PPhXfw":{"type":"subheading","settings":{"subheading":"Our story"}},"heading_Y9MMVQ":{"type":"heading","settings":{"heading":"What if furniture could feel <em>personal<\/em> again?","highlight_style":"thick_underline","highlight_font_style":"normal","highlight_style_color":"#ffe093","highlight_text_color":"","heading_size":"h1"}},"text_7h6LaE":{"type":"text","settings":{"text":"<p>For years, we noticed how most furniture was designed to fit trends, not people. Perfectly smooth. Perfectly repeated. Perfectly forgettable. It filled space, but it didn’t say anything. And it definitely didn’t last — emotionally or physically.<\/p><p><strong>Awefurni <\/strong>began with a simple mission<\/p>","text_size":"text-base","text_line_limit":"none","button_style":"btn--underline","button_icon":"none"}}},"block_order":["subheading_PPhXfw","heading_Y9MMVQ","text_7h6LaE"],"custom_css":[".rich-text {max-width: 88rem; margin: 0 auto;}"],"settings":{"container":"fixed","color_scheme":"","use_color_scheme_in_container":false,"content_spacing":"standard","content_alignment":"center","padding_top":20,"padding_bottom":0,"show_section_divider":false,"divider_width":"fixed"}},"video_hero_HkMiAX":{"type":"video-hero","custom_css":["@media screen and (min-width: 768px) {.video-hero {display: none !important; }}"],"name":"t:sections.video-hero.name","settings":{"container":"full","video":"shopify:\/\/files\/videos\/trailer v4.mp4","video_url":"https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=_9VUPq3SxOc","description":"","video_height":"adapt","overlay_opacity":0,"enable_parallax":false,"parallax_direction":"vertical","color_scheme":"","content_position":"middle-center","content_alignment":"center","video_mobile_height":"adapt","padding_top":50,"padding_bottom":50,"show_section_divider":false,"divider_width":"fixed"}},"image_with_text_eUKGwj":{"type":"image-with-text","blocks":{"badge_AdmYNg":{"type":"badge","settings":{"color_scheme":"scheme-3","text":"Handcrafted Solid Wood Furniture - Awefurni","image":"shopify:\/\/shop_images\/awefurni_favicon.svg","position_mobile":"right"}},"subheading_t37PND":{"type":"subheading","settings":{"subheading":"Every piece starts as an idea — not a template."}},"heading_yrtiRH":{"type":"heading","settings":{"heading":"Design That Doesn’t Repeat","highlight_style":"none","highlight_font_style":"italic","highlight_style_color":"","highlight_text_color":"","heading_size":"h1"}},"text_DycqGr":{"type":"text","settings":{"text":"<p>Creativity helps us explore forms, proportions, and structures that don’t exist in catalogs. Then human hands take over. Skilled woodworkers in Vietnam translate those ideas into real objects, shaping, sanding, and finishing each piece individually.<\/p><p>No two pieces are exactly the same.<br\/>And that’s intentional.<\/p><p>Wood has its own voice — grain lines, knots, subtle imperfections. We don’t erase them. We design around them.<\/p>","subtext_color":true}}},"block_order":["badge_AdmYNg","subheading_t37PND","heading_yrtiRH","text_DycqGr"],"custom_css":[".image-with-text__content {max-width: 52rem;}",".image-with-text__badge .badge__icon {max-width: 8.8rem;}","@media (max-width: 767.98px) {.image-with-text__badge .badge__icon {max-width: 4.5rem; }}"],"settings":{"container":"fixed","color_scheme":"","image":"shopify:\/\/shop_images\/HandcraftedSolidWoodTVStandCabinetWithSculptedWaveFront_5.png","image_position":"left","image_width":50,"desktop_content_position":"center","desktop_content_alignment":"left","mobile_content_alignment":"inherit","show_section_divider":false,"divider_width":"fixed","padding_top":60,"padding_bottom":0}},"image_with_text_XwHBqT":{"type":"image-with-text","blocks":{"subheading_GPjXQt":{"type":"subheading","settings":{"subheading":"The Rhythm of Wood"}},"heading_dVxMFf":{"type":"heading","settings":{"heading":"Where Woodworking isn’t a Factory Process","highlight_style":"none","highlight_font_style":"italic","highlight_style_color":"","highlight_text_color":"","heading_size":"h1"}},"text_7geiy3":{"type":"text","settings":{"text":"<p>It’s a lived skill passed down quietly, over time.<\/p><p>The craftspeople we work with understand wood the way a musician understands sound. They know when to slow down, when to let the material lead, and when not to force perfection.<\/p><p>This is not mass production.<br\/>It’s careful making, one order at a time.<\/p>","subtext_color":true}}},"block_order":["subheading_GPjXQt","heading_dVxMFf","text_7geiy3"],"custom_css":[".image-with-text__content {max-width: 52rem;}"],"settings":{"container":"fixed","color_scheme":"","image":"shopify:\/\/shop_images\/vlcsnap-2026-05-15-17h29m47s510.png","image_position":"right","image_width":50,"desktop_content_position":"center","desktop_content_alignment":"left","mobile_content_alignment":"inherit","show_section_divider":false,"divider_width":"fixed","padding_top":20,"padding_bottom":20}},"image_with_text_wBDMNE":{"type":"image-with-text","blocks":{"subheading_NjWqRE":{"type":"subheading","settings":{"subheading":"We don’t believe sustainability should be loud."}},"heading_a7mGfq":{"type":"heading","settings":{"heading":"Sustainability Done, Not Performed","highlight_style":"none","highlight_font_style":"italic","highlight_style_color":"","highlight_text_color":"","heading_size":"h1"}},"text_qwfaVh":{"type":"text","settings":{"text":"<p><\/p><p>We choose wood responsibly. We avoid waste by making only what is ordered. We finish pieces to last decades, not seasons. No overstock. No disposable design.<\/p><p>Sustainability, to us, means <strong>making fewer things — and making them worth keeping<\/strong>.<\/p>","subtext_color":true}}},"block_order":["subheading_NjWqRE","heading_a7mGfq","text_qwfaVh"],"custom_css":[".image-with-text__content {max-width: 52rem;}",".image-with-text__badge .badge__icon {max-width: 8.8rem;}","@media (max-width: 767.98px) {.image-with-text__badge .badge__icon {max-width: 4.5rem; }}"],"settings":{"container":"fixed","color_scheme":"","image":"shopify:\/\/shop_images\/woman-touching-tree-with-hand.jpg","image_position":"left","image_width":50,"desktop_content_position":"center","desktop_content_alignment":"left","mobile_content_alignment":"inherit","show_section_divider":false,"divider_width":"fixed","padding_top":20,"padding_bottom":20}},"image_with_text_tQktx4":{"type":"image-with-text","blocks":{"subheading_QM8NaH":{"type":"subheading","settings":{"subheading":"It's one of a kind"}},"heading_QmXm4b":{"type":"heading","settings":{"heading":"Furniture With a Point of View","highlight_style":"none","highlight_font_style":"italic","highlight_style_color":"","highlight_text_color":"","heading_size":"h1"}},"text_zhYCrt":{"type":"text","settings":{"text":"<p>This is for people who don’t want their home to look like everyone else’s<\/p><ul><li>For those who notice when something feels <em>considered<\/em>.<\/li><li>For those who value objects with weight, presence, and story.<\/li><li>For those who believe furniture should age with them, not get replaced.<\/li><\/ul><p>If you’re looking for something loud, trendy, or temporary - we may not be the right fit.<\/p><p>But if you’re looking for a piece that quietly becomes part of your life, we’d love to make it for you.<\/p>","subtext_color":true}}},"block_order":["subheading_QM8NaH","heading_QmXm4b","text_zhYCrt"],"custom_css":[".image-with-text__content {max-width: 52rem;}"],"settings":{"